---
// Applies a stored theme preference to <html> before first paint, so
// there's no flash of the wrong theme. Must be the first thing in <head>,
// ahead of the page's own <style> block, and must stay a plain synchronous
// inline script (no defer/module) so it runs during head parsing rather
// than after. Paired with ThemeToggle.astro, which writes the preference
// this reads. One of CLAUDE.md's few named sitewide JS exceptions -
// see docs/decisions.md's dark-mode entry.
//
// Dark is the default as of 2026-09-13 (on request): every page's bare
// :root now defines the dark palette directly, with a
// :root[data-theme="light"] override for the light palette - so dark
// applies even with JS disabled, no attribute needed. This script only
// has to handle the one opt-out case: a visitor who explicitly chose
// light.
---
<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    try {
      if (localStorage.getItem("theme") === "light") {
        document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", "light");
      }
    } catch (e) {}
  })();
</script>
